+#!/usr/bin/env node
+/*
+ * The release queue (PRO current §M.10): the ordered list of candidates whose final battery passed and
+ * which have not reached the main branch. One record per repository, in the git common directory
+ * (<git rev-parse --git-common-dir>/mock2/queue.json), so every worktree reads and writes the same queue.
+ * Every change is written atomically (temporary file, then rename) under the record's lock, the host
+ * budget's slot reservation from check-support.mjs with one slot; nothing here edits a tracked file.
+ *
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs pass <branch> <commit> --battery <runId> [--cache <report.json>] [--base <commit>]
+ *                                [--reserved <id,id…>] [--adopt]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs landed <commit|branch>
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs list [--json]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs base [--for <branch>]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs withdraw <branch> [--reason <text>] [--json]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs absorb <branch> --dry-run|--apply [--records <glob>]… [--json]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs slot take <build|battery|release> [--slots <n>] [--pid <pid>] [-- <command…>]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs slot release <build|battery|release> [--token <token>] [--pid <pid>]
+ *   node .mock2/bin/queue.mjs slot list
+ *   every command takes --main <ref> (else MOCK2_QUEUE_MAIN, else origin/HEAD's branch, origin/main, main,
+ *   master: the main branch as the remote has it when there is one)
+ *
+ * pass      appends a candidate whose final battery passed (branch, commit, battery run, time). A candidate's
+ *           place is fixed when it first passes; a later pass (after a repair or a restack) keeps the place
+ *           and replaces the commit. It is built on the nearest queued candidate whose commit it contains
+ *           (its "parent"), else on the main branch; its base is the parent's tested commit, else the merge
+ *           base with the main branch (--base names it explicitly). A new candidate that lacks the queue tip
+ *           ahead of it is not queued: the tool prints the restack command and exits 1 (§M.10 item 2);
+ *           --adopt queues it anyway, for a repository adopting the queue with candidates already passed.
+ *           --cache reads the battery's run report (check.mjs's report, as battery.mjs copies it to
+ *           .mock2/evidence/<commit>/<runId>.json): a report whose verdict is neither pass nor
+ *           known-baselines-only is refused (exit 1). Its passing results with a fingerprint become the
+ *           entry's "cache" list, each cache file copied to <common>/mock2/cache/<key>.json, so a later
+ *           battery can be seeded from the queue (battery.mjs --seed-cache-from queue):
+ *             cache: [{ "check": "<check id>", "key": "<cache key = fingerprint>", "fingerprint": "<same>",
+ *                       "runId": "<the run that executed it: originalRunId when reused, else the report's>",
+ *                       "file": "<absolute path of the copied cache file, or of the worktree's when the copy
+ *                                is missing>" }]
+ *           Entries a report lists in its own "cache" array (same fields) are taken as they are.
+ *           --reserved records IDs the candidate reserved (rule, decision, work-item IDs), which withdraw
+ *           reports.
+ * landed    removes the entry the release step landed (by its commit, its re-pinned commit or its branch),
+ *           and records its wait (queued → landed) in the record's landed list (§M.10 item 7).
+ * list      the depth and, per entry, its place, branch, commit, battery run, wait so far, what it was built
+ *           on and any restack or re-pin noted; then the landed count and median wait.
+ * base      prints the commit a new build starts from (stdout: the sha alone; stderr: what it is): the queue
+ *           tip, which is the newest queued candidate's commit (the last passed candidate), else the main
+ *           branch's tip. --for <branch> of a queued candidate prints the tip ahead of it instead (the
+ *           previous entry's commit, else the main branch's tip): what it restacks onto before its final
+ *           battery. --for a branch not in the queue prints the queue tip.
+ * withdraw  removes a candidate and names every queued candidate whose commit contains it, with the exact
+ *           restack command for each: `git rebase --onto <withdrawn base> <withdrawn tip> <dependant>` for
+ *           a direct dependant, `git rebase --onto <its parent branch> <the parent's tested commit>
