--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/mock2/templates/repo/.mock2/generators/migration-guard/migration-guard.mjs.tpl
@@ -0,0 +1,373 @@
+/*
+ * The deploy's migration guard, as a module the deploy and a test both run (PRO current §N.11). Generated by
+ * gen.mjs migration-guard; project-owned from now on.
+ *
+ * It PARSES each migration into statements (strings, quoted identifiers, dollar-quoted bodies and comments
+ * are read as what they are, never matched as text) and decides each statement by its form:
+ *   allowed, the lock-friendly forms §N.1 recommends:
+ *     - a constraint added NOT VALID, and VALIDATE CONSTRAINT in a later migration;
+ *     - an index built CONCURRENTLY (or any index on a table this migration creates);
+ *     - a column dropped from NOT NULL (an expand step), a default set or dropped;
+ *     - new tables (not PARTITION OF an existing parent); a column added as `ADD [COLUMN] [IF NOT EXISTS] name
+ *       type` with only NULL, COLLATE, a constant or stable DEFAULT, and NOT NULL beside such a DEFAULT; types, enum values, schemas,
+ *       sequences, views, functions, extensions and comments; lock_timeout / statement_timeout settings;
+ *     - UNIQUE / PRIMARY KEY added USING INDEX (an index built concurrently first);
+ *     - data changes (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) in a migration classified transition;
+ *     - DROP and TRUNCATE in a migration classified contraction or destructive (its approval is checked
+ *       in the manifest);
+ *   Beyond the guard (a reviewed limit): a column whose type is a domain defined elsewhere with a volatile
+ *     default; CREATE DOMAIN … DEFAULT in a migration is refused, so such a domain is reviewed where it is made.
+ *   refused: any other ADD (serial types, quoted or not, volatile or sequence defaults, GENERATED columns, inline UNIQUE,
+ *     PRIMARY KEY, CHECK or REFERENCES, NOT NULL without a DEFAULT, ADD CONSTRAINT … NOT NULL without NOT VALID),
+ *     CREATE TABLE … PARTITION OF (an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock on the parent), a type change (a rewrite), SET NOT NULL (a scan under an exclusive lock), a constraint that
