+ * functions now() and transaction_timestamp() (no rewrite since PostgreSQL 11). Any other call, by a bare,
+ * quoted or schema-qualified name (nextval, gen_random_uuid, uuidv4, uuidv7, random, clock_timestamp, …), is
+ * refused: a volatile default rewrites the table, and a function the guard does not know is not proved
+ * constant. A quoted name is compared as PostgreSQL does, case-sensitively. */
