+  change affects; a visual change runs the affected harness states, not the suite. The final battery
+  is the one full run (§M.10, §M.11).
+- **Repeated load-dependent failures are named for repair.** A failure attributed to load without an
+  entry or a fix is recorded in the handoff with its test id and repeat count. The second time the same
+  test is so attributed it is named for repair; a third dismissal needs either a known-failures entry
+  proved under contention (by exact figures) or the fix (a review finding, not a stop). "Passes alone"
+  is not evidence for a failure that occurs only under load. The runner prints a WARNING for a test id
+  that fails again within its recent runs with no covering entry.
