+{{!
+The release-prompt template (1.42.0, PRO current §P). Filled only by
+  node .mock2/bin/gen.mjs release-prompt --shape image|push|records
+which reads the identity from the release queue's record and the pin, never from an earlier prompt.
+Lines between a shape or if marker and its end marker stay only for that shape or when that value is
+set; markers and this comment never reach the filled prompt. The gate blocks follow gates.mjs's format
+(node .mock2/bin/gates.mjs --help); a done-when: line followed straight away by readonly: true is
+read-only, the only kind a dry run executes. Project-specific commands come from
+.mock2/release-prompt.json.
+}}
+# Release prompt — {{release}} ({{shapeTitle}})
+
+**Status: DRAFT — do not run.** Mark it READY (replace this line with `**Status: READY.**`) only after
+step 0 has dry-run in a scratch clone (`node .mock2/bin/gates.mjs {{promptFile}} --section 0 --dry-run`,
+PRO current §P.6) and the change record holds no placeholder. A prompt that has partly run is marked
+"do not run again" and names its successor (§P.5).
+
+## Identity
+
+Generated {{generated}} by `gen.mjs release-prompt --shape {{shape}}` from {{source}}. Filled from the
+queue record and the pin only; no earlier prompt was read, and every release-time marker below is
+derived from {{markerSource}} by a command in this prompt, never copied (§P.1).
+
+- **Shape:** {{shapeTitle}}
+- **Release:** {{release}}
+- **Candidate branch:** {{branch}}
+- **Pin:** {{pin}}
+- **Commit window:** {{base}}..{{pin}} (commit count {{windowCount}})
+- **Destination:** {{remote}}/{{destBranch}} at {{destinationAt}} when generated
+- **Final battery:** {{battery}}
+- **Shared checkout:** {{repository}}
+- **Change record:** {{changeRecord}}
+- **Records allowed list:** {{allowed}}
+- **Other sessions' record edits accepted at step 0 (§N.8):** {{others}}
+- **Supersedes:** {{supersedes}}
+
+## How to run this prompt
+
+Run each step's gates in order with `node .mock2/bin/gates.mjs {{promptFile}} --section` and the step's number. A gate
+fails only on a non-zero exit of a release command or an unmet `expect:` (§P.2); correct your own shell
+or path errors and run the step again. On a failure, quote the gate runner's output and stop. A value
+one command produces and a later command uses is saved by the runner (`SAVE`, read back as
+`${SAVED:NAME}`), never left in a shell variable; a guard rejects placeholder text as well as an empty
+value (§P.2, §P.3). Exit 3 from the gate runner means the step's `done-when:` holds: it is already done,
+go on to the next. A step is never run out of order except with `--resume`, which this prompt names
+where it allows one.
+
+Never, in this run (§P.2):
+
+- promote, roll back, or change the public release or scheduled jobs;
+- edit system configuration, environment files or units;
+- choose a slot that the controller chooses;
+- touch other worktrees;
+- stage any path not on the records allowed list.
+
+Report in this order (§P.2): the ledger row first, then each step's gate output verbatim (the `report:`
+lines included), the release identity{{reportIdentity}}, the merge output, and the records commit.
+
+### Standing rules (§P.3)
+
+- Start with `cd {{repository}} && date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`; the time goes in the ledger row.
+- Never probe a tool with `--help` when its subcommands act: the probe may run them.
+- Use no pager (`git --no-pager`, `GIT_PAGER=cat`).
+- Assume no optional tool this prompt does not name (use `grep`; `rg` may be absent).
+- Write one ledger row per run of this prompt (each run is its own turn), including a failed one,
+  quoting the line that stopped it.
+- On a failure, quote the error and stop. A refused guard is never bypassed, retried as the same
+  deploy or recovered by privileged improvisation (§N.9): check read-only what landed, commit no
+  record that claims success, report the exact state and wait for the developer.
+- Run `git diff --cached --check` before the records commit, and end every records file with exactly
+  one newline.
+- Put options before `--` in `git commit --only`.
+- Commands reach a resource the way the repository's own scripts do: the same privilege wrapper, the
+  same quoting; database statements go through standard input.
+
+{{#shape image}}
+## Step 0 — preconditions (generated; dry-run before READY)
+
+Checks before anything changes (§N.8, §P.1, §P.7). Any difference stops without touching anything.
+
+```gate
+gate: start
+readonly: true
+SAVE STARTED=date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ
+note: the run's start time, for the ledger row
+gate: pin-exists
+run: git cat-file -e {{pin}}^{commit}
+readonly: true
+gate: candidate-pushed
+run: git ls-remote {{remote}} refs/heads/{{branch}}
+readonly: true
+expect: /^{{pin}}\s/
+note: the candidate branch holds the pinned commit (§N.7 item 1); otherwise the pin is stale: stop
+gate: window
+run: git rev-list --count {{base}}..{{pin}}
+readonly: true
+expect: {{windowCount}}
+gate: destination-unmoved
+run: git ls-remote {{remote}} refs/heads/{{destBranch}}
+readonly: true
+expect: /^{{destinationAt}}\s/
+note: moved since the pin: only the move §M.10 absorbs may continue (the release queue's absorb dry run decides); anything else stops
+gate: deploy-inputs-clean
+run: git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no -- . ':(exclude)state'
+readonly: true
+expect: /^$/
+gate: candidate-adds-untracked
+run: git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A -z {{base}} {{pin}} | xargs -0 -r git ls-files --others --exclude-standard --
+readonly: true
+expect: /^$/
+note: a file the candidate adds exists untracked here; the switch would refuse (§N.8). A byte-identical standards-upgrade copy is staged first (§M.9)
+{{vendoredGates}}gate: change-record-ready
+run: node .mock2/bin/records.mjs placeholders {{changeRecord}} --at {{pin}}
+readonly: true
+note: the change record holds no placeholder for an unfinished check or review (§P.4)
+gate: battery-free
+run: d="${MOCK2_BATTERY_DIR:-{{batteryDir}}}"; i=0; while [ -n "$(ls -A "$d" 2>/dev/null)" ]; do [ -n "$MOCK2_GATES_DRY_RUN" ] && { echo "dry run: a battery is running ($(ls -A "$d")); not waiting"; exit 0; }; i=$((i+1)); [ "$i" -gt {{batteryWaitMinutes}} ] && { echo "battery still running: $(ls -A "$d")"; exit 1; }; sleep 60; done
+readonly: true
+note: waits up to {{batteryWaitMinutes}} minutes for a running final battery (§P.7); after any wait re-run destination-unmoved before going on. A dry run reports a running battery and does not wait
+gate: rollback-slot-decision
+run: awk '{gsub(/<!--.*-->/, "")} /<!--/{c=1} !c{print} /-->/{c=0}' state/decisions.md | grep -E -i '^\|[^|]+\|[^|]+\|[[:space:]]*ACTIVE([[:space:]][^|]*)?\|[[:space:]]*{{rollbackDecisionRe}}'
+readonly: true
+note: an ACTIVE row of the decision ledger whose Decision cell starts "{{rollbackDecision}}" says whether a candidate deploy may replace the slot holding the previous release (§K.3); prose and rows inside an HTML comment (the template's example) do not count. Cite it in the release record. Absent, or this release exceeds it: stop and ask the developer that one question, record the answer in state/decisions.md, then resume at this step
+gate: others-unchanged
+run: node .mock2/bin/records.mjs others --verify {{others}}
+readonly: true
+note: other sessions' record edits named in Identity, unchanged; any other uncommitted record stops. In a scratch clone the listed paths are absent, so a dry run there reports them; nothing else
+```
+
+## Step 1 — switch the deploy checkout to the candidate (§N.7 item 2)
+
+```gate
+gate: fetch-candidate
+run: git fetch --no-tags {{remote}} {{branch}}
+gate: switch
+run: git switch --detach {{pin}}
+gate: at-pin
+run: git rev-parse HEAD
+readonly: true
+expect: {{pin}}
+```
+
+## Step 2 — preflight
+
+```gate
+gate: preflight
+run: {{preflightCmd}}
+```
+
+## Step 3 — build the image at the pin and derive its markers
+
+Every marker is derived from the image this step builds at the pin (§P.1); none is written by hand.
+
+```gate
+gate: build
+run: {{buildCmd}}
+{{markerSaves}}```
+
+## Step 4 — deploy the private candidate
+
+```gate
+gate: deploy
+run: {{deployCmd}}
+{{#if statusCmd}}
+gate: status
+run: {{statusCmd}}
+{{/if}}
+```
+
+## Step 5 — effects of the deploy (§N.8)
+
+A zero exit or a migration runner's "applied" is not evidence; the running container is.
+
+```gate
+{{runningGates}}gate: environment-mode
+readonly: true
+SAVE ENV_MODE={{environmentModeCmd}}
+note: the environment mode read from the running container goes in the release record as written (§E)
+{{effectGates}}```
+
+## Step 6 — real-path smoke of new cross-site or embedded flows (§N.7)
+
+Flows this release adds or alters: {{smokeFlows}}.
+
+Who runs it: {{smokeRunner}}. A real browser with a fresh profile starts each flow where users start it
+(the link, then the page that embeds it, in a cross-site frame where it is framed) on the private
+candidate, before the merge, and sees the expected end state. The change record states the result as
+`real-path smoke: pass`, `real-path smoke: fail` or `real-path smoke: missing` with who ran it and when
+(`real-path smoke: not applicable` when no such flow changed). Not run is `missing`, never a pass.
+
+## Step 7 — merge (§N.7 item 4)
+
+Only on success so far, and only if the destination has not moved since the pin.
+
+```gate
+gate: destination-unmoved
+run: git ls-remote {{remote}} refs/heads/{{destBranch}}
+readonly: true
+expect: /^{{destinationAt}}\s/
+gate: push-destination
+run: git push {{remote}} {{pin}}:refs/heads/{{destBranch}}
+gate: return-to-destination
+run: git fetch --no-tags {{remote}} {{destBranch}} && git switch {{destBranch}} && git merge --ff-only {{pin}}
+gate: at-destination
+run: git rev-parse HEAD
+readonly: true
+expect: {{pin}}
+gate: delete-candidate-branch
+run: git push {{remote}} --delete {{branch}}
+```
+
+## Step 8 — records (§P.4)
+
+In the shared checkout, re-read each file before editing it, then write: one handoff entry naming
+{{release}}; one run-history line in `state/work.md`; exactly one ledger row (the next integer, its
+release cell {{release}}); and in {{changeRecord}} the release identity (the markers the runner saved in
+step 3), `environment mode read from the running container: ` followed by the value step 5 saved,
+the `real-path smoke: ` result, and the rollback-slot decision cited.
+
+```gate
+gate: others-unchanged
+run: node .mock2/bin/records.mjs others --verify {{others}} --own {{allowed}}
+readonly: true
+gate: records-commit
+run: node .mock2/bin/records.mjs commit --allowed {{allowed}} --require "{{changeRecord}}=environment mode read from the running container: ${SAVED:ENV_MODE}" --require "{{changeRecord}}=real-path smoke: " --require "state/run-ledger.md={{release}}" --require "state/handoff.md={{release}}" --base {{remote}}/{{destBranch}} --message "{{message}}"
+raw-saved: true
+note: ENV_MODE is printed as the running container reports it and may hold spaces; records.mjs receives it as one argument and no second shell reads it
+gate: push-records
+run: git push {{remote}} HEAD:refs/heads/{{destBranch}}
+```
+
+## Step 9 — only if the candidate is promoted during the release (§P.8)
+
+Run this step (`--resume 9`) only when the developer promotes the candidate while this prompt runs. It
+never promotes or rolls back. Record as the promotion the developer's own words, or the deployment
+history entry, in the change record. Then replace the private-candidate checks not yet run with their
+public equivalents (the same gates against the public release), and continue to the merge (step 7,
+`--resume 7`) and the records (step 8). Any public identity other than the pinned candidate's image
+stops the run (§N.9). A promotion before step 3 saved the marker cannot be verified: stop and ask.
+
+```gate
+gate: public-identity
+run: {{publicIdentityCmd}}
+readonly: true
+expect: ${SAVED:{{publicMarker}}}
+note: the public release is the pinned candidate's image
+SAVE PROMOTION_SEEN=date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ
+```
+{{/shape}}
+{{#shape push}}
