+# Mock2 1.42.0: lessons from one application's release train
+
+Status: CANDIDATE, NOT PUBLISHED. Smoke-tested; publication waits for the developer's decision. Authorized by the
+developer on 2026-10-29 (`state/work.md`, Authorized scope: release-train lessons (1.42.0), then provider-scoped model
+tiers (1.43.0)). Baseline: published 1.40.0, every one of its 289 release files checked against `release.json`
+before edits. The 1.41.0 lessons release this one was written to follow has not landed; its number stays free, and
+the proposals that built on it are self-contained here (the queue record lives in the git common directory; the port
+helper takes the port explicitly; the local git adapter's 1 MiB buffer is raised to 64 MiB for the archive step).
+
+## Why
+
+One host ran one application through a release train with a coordinating agent, background build, review and release
+agents, and the developer promoting. The time went, in order, to the browser suite in every final battery, full runs
+before review, production differing from what the tests ran, hand-copied release prompts and unhandled release
+states. Every gap was still open in 1.40.0.
+
+## What changes
+
+- **Final batteries (P1):** a build declares an `identity` (never `reuse`); a consumer with `reuse.buildInputs` is
+  reused without the artifact, and the build is recorded `not applicable — no selected consumer needed its artifact`,
+  neither a pass nor a missing check; any dependant that executes, directly or through other checks, makes the build
+  run first. A build's identity includes its prerequisites'. The runner-owned variables leave the environment
+  fingerprint; `battery.cleanEnv` (off by default) runs the clone with a kept list and names what it drops. A passed
+  battery writes its cache back to the worktree and to its queue entry; `battery.mjs --seed-cache-from worktree|queue`
+  seeds the next clone, and a seeded entry whose fingerprint differs from the recomputed key is a named miss. A file
+  that is the slowest and over half its check in three runs running is named for repair.
+- **Runner (P3, P12):** `check.mjs` rechecks the candidate after each shared check and reports heavy checks not yet
+  started as not run, naming the first changed path (`--no-early-stop` keeps the old report); a failure without a
+  known-failures entry that repeats within 10 runs is a WARNING.
+- **Briefs (P2, P16):** the `Checks:` line defaults to no full run before review; `doctor --brief` lints briefs;
+  `port.mjs` reads `HARNESS_PORT` or `.mock2/.local/harness-port` and fails closed.
+- **Release tools (P7–P11, P13):** `gates.mjs` (gate blocks, `${SAVED:NAME}` passed as an environment variable, a
+  safe character set for saved values unless `raw-saved: true`, placeholder refusal before anything runs, a dry run
+  that executes only read-only lines, `done-when`, ordered sections); `records.mjs commit|others|placeholders`;
+  `queue.mjs pass|landed|list|base|withdraw|absorb|slot`; `.mock2/templates/release-prompt.md` filled by
+  `gen.mjs release-prompt --shape image|push|records`, with the real-path smoke step, the promoted-during-release
+  branch, other sessions' records at step 0, the environment mode read back and the rollback-slot decision.
+- **Generator templates (P5, P14, P15):** `non-app-paths` (one list, the worker's denylist generated from it, a drift
+  test), `migration-guard` (manifest `<file> | sha256:<hex> | <classification> | <approval reference> | <lock
+  footprint>`, a statement-parsing guard that refuses any form it does not recognise and allows the lock-friendly
+  ones), `readonly-query` (a host-side helper, screened before connecting, run inside `BEGIN READ ONLY … ROLLBACK`).
+- **Worktree closeout (P20):** `worktree-lifecycle archive-evidence` copies and verifies evidence; a later plan treats
+  those files as preserved while their bytes still match.
+- **Text:** PRO current §E, §F, §K.3, §K.6, §M.4, §M.5, §M.10, §M.11, §N.1, §N.5, §N.7, §N.8, §N.11, §P.1–§P.6 and
+  new §P.8; constitution §1 and §11; rules verification, PRO, security and production checklist; capacity §10, §13,
+  §16; the handoff and decisions templates; the entry block.
+- **Repository tools and tests outside the release:** `scripts/release-smoke.sh` points only install.sh's
+  base-setting line (1.40.0 added a normalizing `BASE=` line, which failed eight smoke cases on the published tree);
+  the names fixture allows the three documentation hosts the stack table has published since 1.39.0; the §K.2 test
+  reads the 1.32.0 amendment as the previous one, as 1.39.0 made it.
+
+No new gate. Every new refusal is a tool refusing its own action; every new warning leaves exit statuses unchanged. No
+project's own settings change: `checks.json` gains examples only in the template.
+
+## Runs
+
+Coordinator plus background builders in separate worktrees with disjoint ownership (runner and battery; brief linter,
+port and archive; gate runner, records tool and release template; release queue and generator templates; standards
+text). Model attribution: not published. Independent review in a separate context: 1 HIGH, 4 MEDIUM, 7 LOW, NITs;
+all fixed; a second reviewer confirmed them and found 1 HIGH (guard bypasses through quoted names, casts and domains,
+reproduced on a real database) and 2 MEDIUM-or-lower; fixed and confirmed closed; its last two findings (a LOW and a
+NIT in the release template) fixed by the coordinator with a test each.
+
+## Checks
+
+Node 24.22.2 (Node 22 lacks `crypto.argon2`), Python 3, Linux.
+
+- Generator: "v1.42.0 — 256 repo-template entries, 255 template identities, release.json covers 307 managed files";
+  a second run changes nothing.
+- Final battery, full suite on the tested commit: 574 tests, 565 pass, 0 fail, 9 skipped (compiler-bridge cases,
+  PowerShell 7, one battery case, the real-database helper case without `MOCK2_TEST_PG`). Baseline 1.40.0: 470 tests,
+  452 pass, 10 fail (eight smoke cases, public hosts, the §K.2 test), 8 skipped.
+- `secrets-coverage.mjs` 31/31; `install-binary.py` PASS; `relay-upgrade.py` PASS.
+- Secret scan of the outgoing commits against 1.40.0: 24,869 added lines in 80 files, nothing found.
+- Release smoke against the candidate served locally, earlier release the live 1.40.0 site: machine install 307/307,
+  repo-init 256/256, updater 1.40.0 → 1.42.0 with a project edit kept, hooks: 4 of 4 PASS.
+- L42-3 measured vs target: the early-stop recheck on 60,000 tracked files took a median 0.87 s and, rerun later on a
+  busier host, 1.09 s (target under 2 s): PASS.
+- Not run: Windows and macOS smoke; the names check with the private list (`MOCK2_PRIVATE_NAMES`); the read-only
+  helper's real-database case on PostgreSQL 18 (it ran on 16.15).
+
+Docs consulted: Node `child_process` (spawnSync `maxBuffer`, `env`) for Node 24; PostgreSQL 18 `ALTER TABLE`,
+`CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` and `SET TRANSACTION READ ONLY` for the guard and helper templates.
+
+## Acceptance
+
