+| L42-1 | `battery-reuse.test.mjs` (write-back, reuse without the build, named misses, failed battery, validator, cleanEnv, queue end to end, transitive dependants, identity chain), slow-file case |
+| L42-2 | `brief-lint.test.mjs`; `release-train-text` L42-2 |
+| L42-3 | `early-stop.test.mjs`; measured vs target above |
+| L42-4 | `release-train-text` L42-4; release-prompt field |
+| L42-5 | `sw-prefix.test.mjs`; text |
+| L42-6 | `release-train-text` L42-6 (template smoke step) |
+| L42-7 | `release-prompt.test.mjs` |
+| L42-8 | `gates-runner.test.mjs` |
+| L42-9 | `records-commit.test.mjs` |
+| L42-10 | `release-prompt.test.mjs` (promoted-early gates); §P.8 text |
+| L42-11 | `release-queue.test.mjs` |
+| L42-12 | `repeat-failure.test.mjs`; text |
+| L42-13 | `records-commit.test.mjs` (others) |
+| L42-14 | `migration-guard.test.mjs` (template cases, review bypasses) |
+| L42-15 | `readonly-helper.test.mjs`; §N.5 text |
+| L42-16 | `port-helper.test.mjs` |
+| L42-17 | `release-train-text` L42-17 (rule text; the template has no ratchet code); `ratchet-seed.test.mjs` fixture |
+| L42-18 | `release-train-text` L42-18; `release-prompt.test.mjs` rollback-slot gate |
+| L42-19 | `release-train-text` L42-19; doctor's instruction-file line |
+| L42-20 | `worktree-archive.test.mjs` |
+
+## Open items
+
+- [OPEN: L42-3 target — assumed under 2 s per heavy check on a 60,000-file tree; measured 0.87–1.09 s.]
+- [OPEN: P12 N — assumed 10 runs.]
+- The 1.41.0 lessons release: its proposals 3, 6, 8, 9 and 13 were re-anchored here as self-contained; when it lands,
+  its tools (`reserve.mjs`, `ledger.mjs`) can replace the explicit port and the queue's own record.
+- History records every candidate identity generated while building (harmless: a repository never holds them).
+- Publication: a guest snapshot, the names check with the private list, the smoke with real bytes against the live
+  site, then the publish; the developer decides.
